150:mod tests {

`OpenAiModel::chat(id)` returns an `OpenAiModelBuilder`; `build()` yields a
`Result<OpenAiModel, BuildError>`.

OpenAI does not use provider tool types. It sends the generic schema for every tool. See [Provider tool types](./tools.md#provider-tool-types).
  - `provider` is a wire-format key that one translator owns. It is not the value of `Model::provider()`. Each provider crate that writes provider data exports its key as a `pub const`. The Gemini crate exports `PROVIDER_DATA_KEY` (`"gemini"`). A host can use the key to filter or remove the data.
Image and audio source parts contribute zero. `ContentPart::ProviderData` counts the length of its serialized `data`, because Gemini bills thought signatures as input tokens.
A Gemini 3 turn that has only tool calls also yields a `MessageOutput`. Its message holds only provider data (see `Item::is_provider_data_only()`). It has no text. The core runner, the workflow agents, the CLI, AG-UI and the HTTP DTO text output skip such a message. A custom consumer that prints text must skip it too.

